\description{
Parameters for \code{\link[=synthetic_bulk_cor_matrix]{synthetic_bulk_cor_matrix()}}. Counts
come from a negative binomial with a mean-dispersion trend; co-expression
modules are planted by putting each module's genes on a shared latent factor.
The \code{generator} picks how loadings and factors are drawn, which is what makes
a given dataset a fair or unfair benchmark for a given method: \itemize{
\item \code{"hub_modular"} - LogNormal loadings on a Normal factor. Some genes end
up far more connected than others, so this is the WGCNA-style default. \item
\code{"modular"} - Beta(5, 2) loadings on a Normal factor. Homogeneous
within-module correlation and no hubs. \item \code{"non_negative_factor"} -
LogNormal loadings on a Gamma factor. The activity matrix is non-negative by
construction, so NMF has a ground truth it can actually reach. \item
\code{"non_gaussian_factor"} - LogNormal loadings on a Laplace factor.
Non-Gaussian sources satisfy ICA identifiability. }
}
